  "slug": "furthest-north",
  "name": "Furthest North",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Furthest North is a twice-yearly furry camping trip and convention in Alberta, Canada, founded in 2001 by Boar-Ral (Thallanor Rasmuson). It began as the West Canadian Furry Campout and was renamed after \"FURther North\" was found to be in use. Furthest North Winter usually takes place over the Alberta Family Day long weekend in February, and Furthest North Summer over the August Civic Holiday weekend. Summer events have been held at provincial recreation areas and, since 2017, at the Snow Creek Group Campground near Rocky Mountain House. Campers must be over 18 unless accompanied by an adult parent or guardian.",
